 324:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** /** @defgroup UARTEx_Exported_Functions_Group3 Peripheral Control functions
 325:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   * @brief    Extended Peripheral Control functions
 326:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   *
 327:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** @verbatim
 328:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****  ===============================================================================
 329:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****                       ##### Peripheral Control functions #####
 330:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****  ===============================================================================
 331:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     [..] This section provides the following functions:
 332:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_UARTEx_EnableClockStopMode() API enables the UART clock (HSI or LSE only) during stop 
 333:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_UARTEx_DisableClockStopMode() API disables the above functionality
 334:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_MultiProcessorEx_AddressLength_Set() API optionally sets the UART node address
 335:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****          detection length to more than 4 bits for multiprocessor address mark wake up.
 336:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_UARTEx_StopModeWakeUpSourceConfig() API defines the wake-up from stop mode
 337:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****          trigger: address match, Start Bit detection or RXNE bit status.
 338:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_UARTEx_EnableStopMode() API enables the UART to wake up the MCU from stop mode
 339:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_UARTEx_DisableStopMode() API disables the above functionality
 340:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_UARTEx_EnableFifoMode() API enables the FIFO mode
 341:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_UARTEx_DisableFifoMode() API disables the FIFO mode
 342:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_UARTEx_SetTxFifoThreshold() API sets the TX FIFO threshold
 343:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_UARTEx_SetRxFifoThreshold() API sets the RX FIFO threshold
 344:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** 
 345:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     [..] This subsection also provides a set of additional functions providing enhanced reception
 346:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     services to user. (For example, these functions allow application to handle use cases
 347:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     where number of data to be received is unknown).
 348:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** 
 349:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     (#) Compared to standard reception services which only consider number of received
 350:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****         data elements as reception completion criteria, these functions also consider additional ev
 351:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****         as triggers for updating reception status to caller :
 352:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****        (+) Detection of inactivity period (RX line has not been active for a given period).
 353:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****           (++) RX inactivity detected by IDLE event, i.e. RX line has been in idle state (normally 
 354:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****                for 1 frame time, after last received byte.
 355:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****           (++) RX inactivity detected by RTO, i.e. line has been in idle state
 356:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****                for a programmable time, after last received byte.
 357:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****        (+) Detection that a specific character has been received.
 358:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** 
 359:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     (#) There are two mode of transfer:
 360:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****        (+) Blocking mode: The reception is performed in polling mode, until either expected number 
 361:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            or till IDLE event occurs. Reception is handled only during function execution.
 362:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            When function exits, no data reception could occur. HAL status and number of actually re
 363:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            are returned by function after finishing transfer.
 364:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****        (+) Non-Blocking mode: The reception is performed using Interrupts or DMA.
 365:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            These API's return the HAL status.
 366:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            The end of the data processing will be indicated through the
 367:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            dedicated UART IRQ when using Interrupt mode or the DMA IRQ when using DMA mode.
 368:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            The HAL_UARTEx_RxEventCallback() user callback will be executed during Receive process
 369:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            The HAL_UART_ErrorCallback()user callback will be executed when a reception error is det
 370:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** 
 371:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     (#) Blocking mode API:
 372:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****         (+) HAL_UARTEx_ReceiveToIdle()
ARM GAS  /var/tmp//ccigKeuX.s 			page 8


 373:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** 
 374:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     (#) Non-Blocking mode API with Interrupt:
 375:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****         (+) HAL_UARTEx_ReceiveToIdle_IT()
 376:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** 
 377:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     (#) Non-Blocking mode API with DMA:
